draft-test.json
C3 131 A CircuitBreaker created with empty Settings has empty name, maxRequests 1, interval 0, timeout 60s, non-nil readyToTrip, nil onStateChange, state StateClosed, zero Counts, and zero expiry.
C4 147 A CircuitBreaker created from custom settings retains the configured name, MaxRequests, Interval, Timeout, and a non-nil OnStateChange, starting in StateClosed with zero Counts and non-zero expiry.
C7 182 In StateClosed, reaching 6 consecutive failures trips the breaker to StateOpen and clears Counts to zero, with expiry set non-zero.
C9 195 While StateOpen, after 59s of pseudoSleep the state remains StateOpen; after an additional 1s (over Timeout) the state transitions to StateHalfOpen and expiry is zeroed.
C11 210 Sequence: after another 60s of pseudoSleep, StateOpen transitions to StateHalfOpen with expiry zeroed; then a success transitions StateHalfOpen to StateClosed with cleared Counts and zero expiry.
C17 290 TwoStepCircuitBreaker mirrors CircuitBreaker state transitions for failure/success flows: counting failures, tripping at 6 consecutive failures, open-to-halfopen after timeout, halfopen-to-open on failure, and halfopen-to-closed on success.
